accuracy. The better move was to move a bishop to a more active position.} 25. Bxf6+ {After all captures, this is an equal trade.} Kxf6 {Kxf6 is best. This maintains the balance in material with a good trade.} 26. fxg5+ {This is an equal trade .} hxg5 {hxg5 is best . After all captures, this is an equal trade.} 27. Rxd6 {Rxd6 is great move. Great find! This was the only move that works! This maintains the balance in material with a good trade} Rxd6 {Rxd6 is best . A straightforward recapture.} 28. c4 {c4 is great. This threatens to win a pawn through an eventual fork.} Ke7 {Ke7 is excellent. One of the best move .} 29. Qe3 {By stacking pieces, white improves coordination} f6 {f6 is best . This defend the attacked pawn .} 30. h4 {This threatens to capture a pawn and win material after the follow-up trades.} gxh4 {gxh4 is best . This is an equal trade.} 31. gxh4 {gxh4 is best . A clear recapture.} Qd7 {Qd7 is mistake. This misses a better way to move a queen to a more active position. This permits the opponent to take an open file with a rook .} 32. Qh6 {Qh6 is a miss. The better move was to take an open file with a rook .} e5 {e5 is an inaccuracy. There were worse moves, but also something much better} 33. h5 {h5 is mistake. This permits the opponent to win a pawn through a fork .} Qg4 {Qg4 is a great move. Black will be winning a pawn with that fork .} 34. Qh7+ {Qh7+ is best . This is the strongest option.} Kd8 {Kd8 is a mistake. The best option was to block a check from the opposing queen.} 35. h6 {This move steps the pawn out of danger and keeps material balance} Rd2 {Rd2 is best . This places the rook on the seventh rank, where it can be highly active} 36. Qf5 {Qf5 is mistake. White had an advantage, but now the game is close to equal.} Qxf5 {Qxf5 is miss. The better move was to defend a pawn that was under attack.} 37. Bxf5 {A CLEAR RECAPTURE} Bd7 {Bd7 is excellent. This moves the bishop to a better location, allowing it to control more squares.} 38. Bg6 {Bg6 is a mistake. The better move was to counterattack an opposing rook. This permits the opponent to use a rook to counter a passed pawn} Rh2 {Rh2 is a great move. Only one good move here, and you spotted it! Placing a rook behind an opposing passed pawn can inhibit the pawn’s ability to promote.} 39. h7 {This move steps the pawn out of danger and keeps material balance.} Ke7 {Ke7 is excellent. This activates the king in the endgame by getting it off of the back rank.} 40. Bd3 {Bd3 is mistake. The best option was to take an open file with a rook.} Be6 {Be6 is miss. The best option was to push a passed pawn. This permits the opponent to move a bishop to a more active position.} 41. Rg1 {Rg1 is a mistake. The best option was to move a bishop to a more active position.} f5 {f5 is a great move. Great find! This was the only move that works! The passed pawn moves towards its goal.} 42. Rg7+ {White reinforces the passed pawn} Kf6 {Kf6 is best . This evades the check from the rook.} 43. Rxa7 {That pawn was free for the taking.} e4 {e4 is best . This kicks the bishop.} 44. Be2 {Be2 is best . This moves the bishop to a better location, allowing it to control more squares.} f4 {f4 is best. Pushing a passed pawn.} 45. b3 {This creates a pawn chain, linked pawns that form a strong structure.} f3 {f3 is best. This kicks the bishop.} 46. Bd1 {This move puts the bishop on a safer square} Bf5 {Bf5 is best . right on target.} 47. Kc1 {Kc1 is excellent. A solid choice.} Bxh7 {Bxh7 is best . That was a free pawn .} 48. Rb7 {Rb7 is excellent. Very strong play.} Ke5 {Ke5 is best . A strong choice !} 49. Rxb6 {This maintains the balance in material with a good trade} Rxa2 {Rxa2 is best . From across the board, Black picks off the pawn.} 0-1